WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.557
In the Gulf, cities drink the sea.

00:00:02.577 --> 00:00:05.040
Yet plants still run on fixed setpoints,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.222
and alarms that fire once the trouble has started.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:09.820
Meet AquaTwin:

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.920
a physics-informed AI digital twin that stays

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.285
calibrated to the plant as it runs.

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:16.640
Physics predicts.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.660
Machine learning corrects the rest.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.178
And every answer carries its uncertainty.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:23.640
Before a salinity shock, it rehearses the day

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.680
ahead. Fixed setpoints break limits for 21 hours.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.667
AquaTwin's plan breaks none.

00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:32.100
It flags membrane fouling half a day before

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.359
cleaning is due.

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:36.660
Its safety layer, AquaGuard, checks every limit,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.420
and outside what the model knows,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.155
it withholds its advice.

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:42.080
Tested against a hidden plant,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.000
fully reproducible, and built for shadow mode on

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.081
data plants already record.

00:00:47.101 --> 00:00:49.866
Smart water, for SDG 6.

00:00:50.026 --> 00:00:50.600
AquaTwin.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.200
Predict, simulate, adapt.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.067
By Team Kanban.
